From: Shimazu <vanessimbolon2020@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 02:19:04 +0000
Subject: ConsoleCommandEffect: Replace Bukkit.getScheduler().runTask with GlobalRegionScheduler

AE PATCH REASON: Bukkit.getScheduler().runTask is rejected by Folia region-threaded architecture and crashes at runtime (UnsupportedOperationException); console command dispatch from async context needs a global scheduler hop.
AE PATCH FIX: Replace Bukkit.getScheduler().runTask with native Bukkit.getGlobalRegionScheduler().run in the off-primary-thread branch.
AE PATCH RISK: LOW - MIGRATE: Bukkit scheduler → GlobalRegionScheduler. No behavior change.

---
diff --git a/net/advancedplugins/ae/impl/effects/effects/effects/internal/ConsoleCommandEffect.java b/net/advancedplugins/ae/impl/effects/effects/effects/internal/ConsoleCommandEffect.java
--- a/net/advancedplugins/ae/impl/effects/effects/effects/internal/ConsoleCommandEffect.java	2026-07-30 10:27:31.665350096 +0000
+++ b/net/advancedplugins/ae/impl/effects/effects/effects/internal/ConsoleCommandEffect.java	2026-07-30 14:05:12.681842947 +0000
@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@
    public boolean executeEffect(ExecutionTask var1, LivingEntity var2, String[] var3) {
       String var4 = String.join(":", var3);
       if (!Bukkit.isPrimaryThread()) {
-         Bukkit.getScheduler().runTask(ASManager.getInstance(), () -> Bukkit.dispatchCommand(Bukkit.getConsoleSender(), var4));
+         Bukkit.getGlobalRegionScheduler().run(ASManager.getInstance(), (t) -> Bukkit.dispatchCommand(Bukkit.getConsoleSender(), var4));
          return true;
       } else {
          Bukkit.dispatchCommand(Bukkit.getConsoleSender(), var4);
